The code statements that lead to the bug are:
dst = page_address(rqstp->rq_pages[head->rc_curpage]);
head->rc_curpage++;
Reason:
The function uses `head->rc_curpage` as an index into `rqstp->rq_pages` without verifying it is less than `rqstp->rq_maxpages`. The index can exceed the allocated array size when processing large inline data or multiple Read chunks, causing an out-of-bounds memory access.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
if (head->rc_curpage >= rqstp->rq_maxpages)
	return -EINVAL;
Reason:
This guard at the beginning of each loop iteration ensures that the index `rc_curpage` is valid before accessing `rqstp->rq_pages[rc_curpage]`. If the index exceeds the maximum number of pages, the function returns an error, preventing out-of-bounds access. The check also protects against the increment of `rc_curpage` later in the loop, because the next iteration will re-validate the new index.

